{"qid":"Q33296","names":["Mughal Empire"],"title":"Mughal Empire","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Mughal Empire was a Persianate Timurid dynasty founded by Babur after his victory at the First Battle of Panipat in 1526, which brought him control of the Delhi Sultanate's territories. Under Akbar (r. 1556–1605) the empire reached its administrative apex, governing most of the Indian subcontinent through a centralized mansabdari system with revenues exceeding any contemporary European state. Aurangzeb (r. 1658–1707) extended the empire to its greatest territorial extent but his exhausting Deccan campaigns and religious policies fractured Mughal authority, and by his death autonomous successor states—the Marathas, the Nawabs of Bengal and Oudh—had effectively fragmented central power. The dynasty survived as a pensioned rump under British suzerainty until the last emperor Bahadur Shah II was exiled to Rangoon following the 1857 uprising.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial extent is well-documented through Mughal administrative records (ain-i-Akbari), imperial farmans, and subsequent colonial surveys; provincial boundaries are accurately attested from the late 16th century onward, though frontier zones in the northwest and Deccan are more approximate.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Mughal dynasty","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Mughal-dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Mughal Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mughal_Empire"}],"britannica":"topic/Mughal-dynasty","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Mughal Empire","rulers":[{"qid":"Q797848","name":"Babur","nativeName":"ظهیرالدین محمد بابر","roman":"Ẓahīr al-Dīn Muḥammad Bābur","start":1526,"end":1530,"image":"Humayun and Babur (Late Shah Jahan Album) Babur detail.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Humayun%20and%20Babur%20(Late%20Shah%20Jahan%20Album)%20Babur%20detail.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"c.1650","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q486188","name":"Humayun","nativeName":"نصیرالدین محمد همایون","roman":"Naṣīr al-Dīn Muḥammad Humāyūn","start":1530,"end":1540,"image":"Humayun and Babur (Late Shah Jahan Album) Humayun detail.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Humayun%20and%20Babur%20(Late%20Shah%20Jahan%20Album)%20Humayun%20detail.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"c.1650","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":null,"name":"Humayun (restored)","nativeName":"نصیرالدین محمد همایون","roman":"Naṣīr al-Dīn Muḥammad Humāyūn","start":1555,"end":1556,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":"Q8597","name":"Akbar","nativeName":"جلال‌الدین محمد اکبر","roman":"Jalāl al-Dīn Muḥammad Akbar","start":1556,"end":1605,"image":"Contemporary seated portrait of Akbar, 1605.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Contemporary%20seated%20portrait%20of%20Akbar%2C%201605.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"1605 artist","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":null,"name":"Jahangir","nativeName":"نورالدین محمد جهانگیر","roman":"Nūr al-Dīn Muḥammad Jahāngīr","start":1605,"end":1627,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":"Q83672","name":"Shah Jahan","nativeName":"شهاب‌الدین محمد شاه جهان","roman":"Shihāb al-Dīn Muḥammad Shāh Jahān","start":1628,"end":1658,"image":"Shah Jahan, in The Rulers of the Mughal Dynasty from Babur to Awrangzeb, with their Ancestor Timur MSS 874, India, circa 1707–12. Khalili Collection.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Shah%20Jaha